ECV. However, for native T2, there was a slight increase in native T2 values in segment 10 (p&#x02009;=&#x02009;0.036) which represents the mid-ventricular inferior wall. Only 1 out of the 67 participants in our cohort demonstrated minor non-specific LGE at the mid-ventricular anterior wall on both 1st and 2nd CMR scans. No new LGE or high T2 signal changes in the myocardium or pericardium were demonstrated on the LGE or T2 STIR images in any of the subjects. No participant fulfilled the updated LLC for myocarditis.<table-wrap id="Tab3"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Cardiac Magnetic Resonance Results Before and After 2 Vaccination Doses (n&#x02009;=&#x02009;67)</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left"/><th align="left">Before 1st vaccine dose</th><th align="left">After 2nd vaccine dose</th><th align="left">p-value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">LV EDV Indexed (ml/m<sup>2</sup>)</td><td align="left">81 <inline-formula id="IEq23"><alternatives><tex-math id="M45">\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
